confirm_push.description:
The connection test to {address} succeeded in push mode: the unit does not answer classic reads with register data, but it answers every request with a live-data report that the integration reads — one request per poll cycle.

What you get in push mode:
- The temperature sensors appear once the captured values are confirmed below (or later in the options).
- The climate entity appears once the power/mode calibration is confirmed below (or later in the options): it shows OFF/HEAT following the unit's power state and the current heat target, read-only.
- Power control (on/off) and setpoint control can be enabled later in the integration's options, each after running its built-in write probe (a diagnostic that verifies the write is executed and reversible).
- The fault code and the firmware version are not available (no data home was identified in the report).

